## 19. AppsFlyer started offline, or started from the wrong place (CRITICAL)

Three distinct bugs with one symptom — **a OneLink install lands in the native
game** — and all three cost a full test cycle each. Full treatment in
`kotlin_launch_flow.mdc`; the short forms:

**19a. Started with no connection.** `start()` runs in `Application.onCreate`,
the device is offline, `onConversionDataFail` fires in milliseconds and the
`CompletableDeferred` completes with an empty map. When the user turns Wi-Fi on
and the router asks again, it gets that cached empty map back in 2 ms, sends a
body with no attribution, and the backend correctly answers 404.

*Tell:* `conversion={}` logged a couple of milliseconds after the decision
started.
*Fix:* connectivity gate before `start`, always. Plus a re-ask and a direct GCD
call as safety nets.

**19b. `init` moved out of the Application.** Fixing 19a by moving the whole
AppsFlyer setup into the router breaks it differently: the SDK learns the app
is in the foreground from `ActivityLifecycleCallbacks` registered during
`init`, so registering them while an activity is already resumed misses the
event. The launch is queued until the *next* activity appears — the native
game, ~32 seconds later.

*Tell:* a 30-second gap, then `onBecameForeground` / `Sending first launch for
this session!`, then the correct conversion, far too late. AppsFlyer's own
payload says `"first_launch":{"init_to_fg":32239}`.
*Fix:* `init` in `Application.onCreate` (sends nothing), `start` in the router.

**19c. `start(applicationContext)` called from an Activity.** Same 30-second
hang. AppsFlyer's guide: *"Failing to pass the activity context will not
trigger the SDK, thus losing attribution data and in-app events."*

*Fix:* `AppsFlyerLib.getInstance().start(activity)`.

---

## 20. First launch offline sends the user to the game — permanently

**Symptom:** OneLink install with the radio off. The app shows the game, and
after Wi-Fi returns it keeps showing the game on every future launch.

**Cause:** the offline branch of the first decision routed to the game, and the
negative verdict was persisted as the mode. The mode is by contract permanent,
so the paid user is locked out for the life of the install.

**Fix:** offline on an undecided first launch → the no-wifi screen **on the
first frame** (instant `activeNetwork` check before `setContentView`), nothing
started, nothing persisted; the offline screen relaunches the router when the
link returns. And persist `NATIVE` only when the endpoint actually answered AND
the request carried attribution (`kotlin_launch_flow.mdc` §4–5).

---

## 21. `onCreateWindow` with the same WebView (CRASH)

**Symptom:** `IllegalArgumentException: Parent WebView cannot host its own
popup window`. Reproduced on the third page of a test site's "next page" chain.

**Cause:** `setSupportMultipleWindows(true)` plus
`transport.webView = view` — the parent WebView cannot be its own popup host.

**Fix:** `setSupportMultipleWindows(false)`; `window.open` then loads in place.
Only if popups are truly required, create a separate throwaway WebView for the
transport and forward its first URL to the main view.

---

## 22. ERR_UNKNOWN_URL_SCHEME on payment / wallet links

**Symptom:** *"Не удалось открыть веб-страницу … paytmmp://pay …
ERR_UNKNOWN_URL_SCHEME"*.

**Cause:** `shouldOverrideUrlLoading` externalized only a hardcoded list of
schemes and let everything unknown fall through to the WebView.

**Fix:** invert it — keep `http/https/about/data/blob/file/javascript` in the
WebView and hand every other scheme to the system with `ACTION_VIEW`
(`intent://` parsed via `Intent.parseUri`, with the `browser_fallback_url`
honoured). Treat `ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_SCHEME` in `onReceivedError` as harmless:
the URL already went to the system, so leave the page where it was.

---

## 23. Black screen between redirects

**Symptom:** tapping a link that redirects: the page zooms out, goes black, and
only then shows the destination.

**Cause:** a "freeze-frame" built with `view.draw(canvas)` to hide the hops. A
hardware-accelerated WebView draws **black** into a software canvas.

**Fix:** never snapshot the view. There is nothing to hide a redirect hop
behind that is better than the page the user is already reading — leave it on
screen and let the destination replace it. See #33 for why covering the hops
was the wrong answer to this in the first place.

---

## 24. Redirect retry budget never runs down

**Symptom:** `ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS` on a chain longer than 20 hops; the retry
"works" but the user still ends up on the native error page.

**Cause:** a failed load still reaches `onPageFinished` with the error page
committed. That handler reset the retry counter and recorded the error URL as
settled, and it also dropped the cover while a reload was queued.

**Fix:** a `loadFailed` flag set in `onReceivedError` and cleared in
`onPageStarted`, and skip the whole `onPageFinished` body when it is set.

That is only half of a working retry — see #30 for the other half, which is
*where* the retry resumes from and *how* it is issued.

---

## 25. The keyboard fix that is in every tutorial does not work

**Symptom:** content jumps higher than needed when the keyboard opens and drops
back a frame later; sometimes fine, sometimes not — "дёргается".

**Cause:** `adjustResize` (or IME padding) plus a JS `scrollIntoView` means the
engine and the injection both scroll the same page, and their corrections add
up.

**Fix:** the pan approach in `kotlin_keyboard.mdc` — strip IME insets from the
WebView, slide the view with `translationY`, clamp to the *settled* keyboard
height (the system over-reports by 45–80 px mid-animation) and remember that
height per orientation across runs.

---

## 26. The loading screen appears twice, or the bar never fills

**Symptom:** the splash is shown on launch, then again before the WebView; the
bar jumps to the next screen at 60%; after granting the notification permission
the splash comes back.

**Cause:** each activity ran its own loading session, and navigation happened
on its own schedule rather than on the bar's.

**Fix:** one session per launch, shared across activities (a process-wide
clock), and a single `complete { … }` gate: the bar runs to 100%, then the
handover happens ~0.5 s later. The permission screen holds until the page
behind it is ready; a warm push draws nothing at all.

---

## 27. JavascriptInterface stripped in release

**Symptom:** everything that talks to the page (keyboard pan, safe-area probe)
works in debug and silently does nothing in a minified build.

**Fix:**
```
-keepclassmembers class * { @android.webkit.JavascriptInterface <methods>; }
```

