## 36. The permission promo comes back after the user accepted it

**Symptom:** The user taps **Accept**, declines in the system dialog, and three
days later the promo is in their face again — offering a button that now does
nothing, because Android will not reopen that dialog.

**Cause:** a three-flag gate — `notifGranted`, `notifOsDenied`, `notifSkipUntil`
— with the outcome decided in the permission callback:

```kotlin
// ❌ the leaky branch
if (granted) vault.notifGranted = true
else {
    val denied = !shouldShowRequestPermissionRationale(POST_NOTIFICATIONS)
    if (denied) vault.notifOsDenied = true
    else vault.snoozeNotifPrompt()      // ← promo returns in 3 days
}
```

`shouldShowRequestPermissionRationale` is the wrong question. It answers whether
Android would *render a rationale*, not whether the dialog will ever open again,
and on the first refusal it can still return true — dropping the user into the
3-day branch. There is a second hole in the same shape: kill the app while the
dialog is up and the callback never fires, so nothing is written down at all.

**Fix:** two states, one flag each, and the decision made on the tap rather than
on the answer.

```kotlin
// DataVault
var notifSkipUntil: Long        // Skip → now + PUSH_SNOOZE_SEC
var notifPromoClosed: Boolean   // Accept → true, forever

fun shouldShowNotifScreen(): Boolean {
    if (notifPromoClosed) return false
    return System.currentTimeMillis() / 1000 >= notifSkipUntil
}

// AlertPortal — before the dialog opens, not in the callback
private fun onAccept() {
    vault.notifPromoClosed = true
    if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT < Build.VERSION_CODES.TIRAMISU) { proceed(); return }
    val already = ContextCompat.checkSelfPermission(this, POST_NOTIFICATIONS) ==
        PackageManager.PERMISSION_GRANTED
    if (already) proceed() else permLauncher.launch(POST_NOTIFICATIONS)
}

private val permLauncher = registerForActivityResult(RequestPermission()) { proceed() }
```

Whichever way the dialog is answered, the promo has nothing left to offer: a
granted permission needs no promo, a refused one cannot be re-requested. Skip
still postpones for three days, unchanged. Drop `notifGranted` and
`notifOsDenied` rather than leaving them in the condition — once the closed flag
is set on the tap they can never independently be true, and a reader will waste
time working out why they are there.

